- (The door you're guarding.)
	merlin: It leads to an ancient hall through which one might access Camlann's lake and thereafter Annwn. The gate may only be opened if it may drink from the Holy Grail.
- (Updated technology)
	merlin: I will not pretend to understand the reasoning behind Camlann's progression or lack thereof. Tell me, is the technology here similar to that you have seen outside?
	It all seems a bit out of date, still. Computers like Gawain's aren't in use unless you like that sort of thing.
	merlin: How interesting. Well, don't tell him he's behind; ever since he learned of computer games, he's been nigh insufferable about it. Pinball is enjoyable enough, but everything becomes tiresome in excess.
- (Ask about the curse?)
	merlin: You know it as well as I, that we shall remain of faire mind and body until our quests have been completed by another.
	Shouldn't I be exempt from that? Galahad completed my quest already.
	merlin: Perhaps there is another quest assigned to you that still remains. These things work without regard for mortal sense.
- (The garden's overgrown...)
	merlin: Well, yes, but it's been like that for some time now. Poor Galahad hasn't had a bit of luck keeping the thing contained, and the water here is very pure.
- (The elevators...)
	merlin: Yes, what of them?
	I can't seem to get to the second or third floors.
	merlin: Ah, yes. That's been an issue for quite some time. Bedivere's been preoccupied with a vermin issue, though I suppose he considers the second floor's issue to be Galahad's responsibility.
- (Bediwyr's beast...) | [if {convo_progress.bedivere.bedivereGreeted} == true] [else="hide"]
	merlin: A beast? Yes, Bedivere has often complained of vermin. I have seen my share of rats here, of course, but I cannot imagine it is these miniscule creatures that bother him so. Galahad purports to have seen it. Have you spoken to him yet?
	if {convo_progress.galahad.galahadGreeted} == false:
		Not yet. He's not the easiest to talk to.
		merlin: You fear your own blood?
		Well, not really...
		merlin: And yet you still hesitate.
		(dialogue branch unfinished)
	elif {questProgress.questingBeast.investigationStatus} == "beastknown":
		I have. He wasn't much help, but he did describe the beast to me.
		merlin: Did he now? What manner of beast is it, then?
		(Describe the beast to Merlin)
		merlin: And this beast, it does not seem familiar to you?
		Only just.
	set {convo_progress.merlin.galahadGossip} = true
- (That dog running around...)
	merlin: Ah, yes, him. Merrok, I believe he is called. A good man, once, now cursed to be a beast.
- I believe that's it.
	if {convo_progress.merlin.merlinGreeted} == false:
		merlin: Of course. I shall remain here to guard the door, so have no fear to return to ask about anything else.
		jump merlinIntro/introEnd
	else:
		merlin: Gods be with you, Ser Percivel.
		[end_timeline]